{"records":[{"id":"ztg7pxr6ch","title":"STT3A is essential for Wnt signaling and represents a target for cancers driven by RNF43 deficiency","description":"This dataset contains the original raw and analyzed data supporting the manuscript “STT3A is essential for Wnt signaling and represents a target for cancers driven by RNF43 deficiency”. The study identifies STT3A as an essential regulator of the Wnt signaling pathway and a potential therapeutic target for RNF43-deficient cancers. Included data were generated from key experiments, including Wnt reporter assays (DDT), Western blotting (WB), and CRISPR screen, and other experiments central to the study","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-10-13T11:26:58.874Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ztg7pxr6ch","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ztg7pxr6ch"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Zhengjin","last_name":"He","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"2v5jg2zksj","title":"TMEM79/MATTRIN defines a pathway for Frizzled regulation and is required for Xenopus embryogenesis","description":"Absctract\nWnt signaling through the Frizzled (FZD) family of serpentine receptors is essential for embryogenesis and homeostasis, and stringent control of the FZD protein level is critical for stem cell regulation. Through CRISPR/Cas9 genome-wide screening in human cells, we identified TMEM79/MATTRIN, an orphan multi-span transmembrane protein, as a specific inhibitor of Wnt/FZD signaling. TMEM79 interacts with FZD during biogenesis and promotes FZD degradation independent of ZNRF3/RNF43 ubiquitin ligases (R-spondin receptors). TMEM79 interacts with ubiquitin-specific protease 8 (USP8), whose activating mutations underlie human tumorigenesis. TMEM79 specifically inhibits USP8 deubiquitination of FZD, thereby governing USP8 substrate specificity and promoting FZD degradation. Tmem79 and Usp8 genes have a pre-bilaterian origin, and Tmem79 inhibition of Usp8 and Wnt signaling is required for anterior neural development and gastrulation in Xenopus embryos. TMEM79 is a predisposition gene for Atopic dermatitis, suggesting deregulation of Wnt/FZD signaling a possible cause for this most common yet enigmatic inflammatory skin disease.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-09-26T05:47:58.606Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/2v5jg2zksj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/2v5jg2zksj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Maorong","last_name":"Chen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nathalia","last_name":"Amado","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jieqiong","last_name":"Tan","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Alice ","last_name":"Reis","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Mengxu","last_name":"Ge","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jose","last_name":"Abreu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xi","last_name":"He","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Biochemistry","Molecular Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xn3vv2cdnk","title":"High-throughput CRISPR screens to dissect macrophage-Shigella interactions","description":"The positive hits, negative hits, and non-targeting controls of genome-wide CRISPR screens; Supplemental Tables.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-07-23T06:18:30.182Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xn3vv2cdnk","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xn3vv2cdnk"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yong","last_name":"LAI","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Genetic Screening","Host-Pathogen Interaction","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"hfbhym45fz","title":"CRISPR screening reveals a requirement for ribosome recycling in efficient SARS-CoV-2 programmed ribosomal frameshifting and viral replication. Rehfeld et al.","description":"Supplemental Table S1. Results of SARS-CoV-2 programmed ribosomal frameshifting genome-wide CRISPR screens (MAGeCK analysis).\nSupplemental Table S2. Oligonucleotides.\n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-01-19T12:17:58.922Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/hfbhym45fz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/hfbhym45fz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Joshua","last_name":"Mendell","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Frederick","last_name":"Rehfeld","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/0003xa228","name":"Cancer Prevention and Research Institute of Texas","grant_id":"RP220309"},{"id":"https://ror.org/00np6vq88","name":"Welch Foundation","grant_id":"I-1961-20210327"},{"id":"https://ror.org/006w34k90","name":"Howard Hughes Medical Institute","grant_id":null}],"categories":["Oligonucleotide","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"k6wm46g4tw","title":"Data set for the paper entitled \"CRISPR-enabled genetic screens identify synthetic lethal targets across frequently altered cancer drivers\" by Desjardins, Bowlan, et al. (2026)","description":"We undertook a series of genome-wide CRISPR screens using functionally validated isogenic cell lines and mapped SL interactions across 15 genetic alterations characteristic of diseases with high incidence and unmet clinical need: FBXW7, CCNE1, CDK12, ARID1A, KMT2D, DNMT3A, TET2, KEAP1, STK11, IDH1, SF3B1, SRSF2, U2AF1, chromosome 18q loss, and chromosome 13q loss. The data deposited here make the raw read count files available for all CRISPR screens conducted in the study. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-01-26T11:43:11.208Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/k6wm46g4tw","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/k6wm46g4tw"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jordan","last_name":"Young","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Alejandro","last_name":"Álvarez-Quilón","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jessica","last_name":"Desjardins","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Julian","last_name":"Bowlan","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Primary Data"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"jvpgmxs3n6","title":"Supplemental material for: \"A genome-wide association meta-analysis links hidradenitis suppurativa to common and rare sequence variants causing disruption of the Notch and Wnt/β-catenin signaling pathways\"","description":"Supplemental material for the manuscript \"A genome-wide association meta-analysis links hidradenitis suppurativa to common and rare sequence variants causing disruption of the Notch and Wnt/β-catenin signaling pathways\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-01-31T13:10:54.026Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/jvpgmxs3n6","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/jvpgmxs3n6"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Rune","last_name":"KjÃ¦rsgaard Andersen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Lilja","last_name":"Stefansdottir","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Peter","last_name":"Riis","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Gisli","last_name":"Halldorsson","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Egil","last_name":"Ferkingstad","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Asmundur","last_name":"Oddsson","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Bragi","last_name":"Walters","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Thorunn","last_name":"Olafsdottir","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Gudrun","last_name":"Rutsdottir","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Claus","last_name":"Zachariae","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Simon","last_name":"Thomsen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Thorsten","last_name":"Brodersen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Khoa","last_name":"Dinh","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kirk","last_name":"Knowlton","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Stacey","last_name":"Knight","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Lincoln","last_name":"Nadauld","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Karina","last_name":"Banasik","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Søren","last_name":"Brunak","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Thomas","last_name":"Hansen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Henerik","last_name":"Hjalgrim","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Erik","last_name":"Sørensen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Christina","last_name":"Mikkelsen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Henrik","last_name":"Ullum","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Mette","last_name":"Nyegaard","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Mie","last_name":"Brunn","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Christian","last_name":"Erikstrup","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sisse","last_name":"Ostrowski","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Liv","last_name":"Eidsmo","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ditte","last_name":"Saunte","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Bardur","last_name":"Sigurgeirsson","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kjartar","last_name":"Ovar","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jona","last_name":"Saemundsdottir","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Pall","last_name":"Melsted","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Gudmundur","last_name":"Norddahl","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Patrick","last_name":"Sulem","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Hreinn","last_name":"Stefansson","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Hilma","last_name":"Holm","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Daniel","last_name":"Gudbjartsson","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Gudmar","last_name":"Thorleifsson","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ingileif","last_name":"Jonsdottir","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ole","last_name":"Pedersen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Gregor","last_name":"Jemec","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kari","last_name":"Stefansson","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/02hcraz70","name":"Aase og Ejnar Danielsens Fond","grant_id":null},{"id":"https://ror.org/02rgsr590","name":"LEO Foundation","grant_id":"LF 18002"},{"id":"https://ror.org/04txyc737","name":"Novo Nordisk Foundation","grant_id":"NNF20SA0064340 "}],"categories":["Genetics","Dermatology","Genome Wide Association Study","Hidradenitis Suppurativa"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"nnxh5d35nd","title":"Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 screen identified KLF11 as a druggable suppressor for sarcoma cancer stem cells","description":"The original, unprocessed data alongside the paper","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-05-31T01:39:45.722Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/nnxh5d35nd","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/nnxh5d35nd"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Le","last_name":"Qu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"n9w7zwc6pn","title":"raw data","description":"P4HB-Positive Classical Monocytes Drive the Sjögren’s Syndrome–Osteoarthritis Axis and Reveal a Druggable P4HB Signaling Network Through Virtual Gene Perturbation and Drug Repurposing","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-07-16T09:57:26.47Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/n9w7zwc6pn","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/n9w7zwc6pn"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"yupei","last_name":"dai","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Medicine","Addiction Medicine"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"9x47wzy8x7","title":"A study of \"Genome-wide CRISPR screens reveal host factors critical for SARS-CoV-2 infection\" by Wei et al. Cell 2020","description":"Identification of host genes essential for SARS-CoV-2 infection may reveal novel therapeutic targets and inform our understanding of COVID-19 pathogenesis. Here, we performed genome-wide CRISPR screens in Vero-E6 cells with SARS-CoV-2, MERS-CoV, bat coronavirus HKU5 expressing the SARS-CoV-1 spike, and VSV expressing the SARS-CoV-2 spike. Together this identifies potential therapeutic targets for SARS-CoV-2 and reveals SARS-lineage specific and pan-coronavirus host factors that regulate susceptibility to highly pathogenic coronaviruses.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-10-15T21:29:14.06Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/9x47wzy8x7","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/9x47wzy8x7"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Craig","last_name":"Wilen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR","Middle East Respiratory Syndrome-Related Coronavirus","Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"pm5v6pwkkg","title":"Genome-wide screens implicate loss of cullin ring ligase 3 in persistent proliferation and genome instability in TP53 deficient cells","description":"TP53 deficiency is the most common alteration in cancer, however, alone is typically insufficient to drive tumorigenesis. To identify genes promoting tumorigenesis in combination with TP53 deficiency, we performed genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 knockout screens coupled with proliferation and transformation assays in isogenic cell lines. Loss of several known tumor suppressor genes enhanced cellular proliferation and transformation. Surprisingly, loss neddylation pathway genes, promoted uncontrolled proliferation exclusively in TP53-deficient cells. CUL3 coupled with TP53 loss results in an oncogenic transcriptional program governed by the NFκB, AP-1 and TGF-β pathways. This program maintains persistent cellular proliferation, induces partial epithelial to mesenchymal transition, increases DNA damage, genomic instability, and the rate chromosomal rearrangements. Our findings reveal CUL3 loss as a key event stimulating persistent proliferation in TP53 deficient cells. These findings may be clinically relevant, since TP53-CUL3 deficient cells are highly sensitive to ATM inhibition, exposing a vulnerability that could be exploited for cancer treatment. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-11-06T17:31:10.704Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/pm5v6pwkkg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/pm5v6pwkkg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Alexandros","last_name":"Drainas","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot","Cellular Imaging"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":130865,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":106,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":130865,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":130322,"restricted":64,"embargoed":479},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2179},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":1386},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":599},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":451},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":438},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":414},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":408},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":362},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":291},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":257}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":128256},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1900},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":181},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":130},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of South Florida","count":73},{"id":"2a9d1b7d-e447-466f-888f-aa6f84e575e4","name":"Digital Commons Data@Becker","count":64},{"id":"72c28c45-627f-446b-8a48-af7c0a51a357","name":"Università Cattoli